  "question": {
    "text": "A square loop of sides $a=1 \\mathrm{~m}$ is held normally in front of a point charge $\\mathrm{q}=1 \\mathrm{C}$. The flux of the electric field through the shaded region is $\\frac{5}{\\mathrm{p}} \\times \\frac{1}{\\varepsilon_0} \\frac{\\mathrm{Nm}^2}{\\mathrm{C}}$, where the value of p is _____.\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/455N9nYH83J-kqdehPYH4ZFDZnCGo9xPSwbp8rnmjwg.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "48",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1PblQ3ZoSOlHnQqVJ9OexMcJKkr6UeL1xQSotIwpu6k.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\n\n\n\nTotal flux through square $=\\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{\\epsilon_0}\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)$\nLets divide square is 8 equal parts.\nFlux is same for each part.\n$\\therefore$ Flux through shaded portion is $\\frac{5}{8}$ (Total flux)\n$=\\frac{5}{8} \\times \\frac{\\mathrm{q}}{\\epsilon_0} \\frac{1}{6}=\\frac{5}{48} \\frac{1}{\\epsilon_0}$\n$\\therefore$ required Ans. is 48",
    "image": null
  },
